{number: 19}
{title: Take the Name of Jesus with You}
{key: Ab}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[Ab] Take the name of Jesus with you,
[Db] Child of sorrow [Ab] and of woe,
It will joy and comfort [Eb] give you,
[Ab] Take it, then, where-[Eb7] e’er you [Ab] go.
Precious [Db] name, O how [Ab] sweet!
Hope of earth and joy of [Eb] heav’n;
Precious [Ab] name, [Ab7] O how [Db] sweet!
[Ab] Hope of earth and [Eb7] joy of [Ab] heav’n.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[Ab] Take the name of Jesus ever,
[Db] As a shield from [Ab] every snare;
If temptations round you [Eb] gather,
[Ab] Breathe that holy [Eb7] name in [Ab] prayer.
Precious [Db] name, O how [Ab] sweet!
Hope of earth and joy of [Eb] heav’n;
Precious [Ab] name, [Ab7] O how [Db] sweet!
[Ab] Hope of earth and [Eb7] joy of [Ab] heav’n.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
[Ab] O the precious name of Jesus!
[Db] How it thrills our [Ab] souls with joy,
When His loving arms re-[Eb] ceive us,
[Ab] And His songs our [Eb7] tongues em-[Ab] ploy.
Precious [Db] name, O how [Ab] sweet!
Hope of earth and joy of [Eb] heav’n;
Precious [Ab] name, [Ab7] O how [Db] sweet!
[Ab] Hope of earth and [Eb7] joy of [Ab] heav’n.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 4}
[Ab] At the name of Jesus bowing,
[Db] Falling prostrate [Ab] at His feet,
King of kings in heav’n we’ll [Eb] crown Him,
[Ab] When our journey [Eb7] is com-[Ab] plete.
Precious [Db] name, O how [Ab] sweet!
Hope of earth and joy of [Eb] heav’n;
Precious [Ab] name, [Ab7] O how [Db] sweet!
[Ab] Hope of earth and [Eb7] joy of [Ab] heav’n.
{end_of_verse}
